WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.421
"Good, you're all here," Morb said, sneering.

2
00:00:16.422 --> 00:00:22.584
"You may have been able to trick those idiotic trolls, but you won't escape from me this time."

3
00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:24.858
"Run!" Perda yelled.

4
00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:28.490
"Not so fast." Morb waved his hand.

5
00:00:28.491 --> 00:00:32.261
A translucent green bubble appeared over the entire house.

6
00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:36.226
Perda skidded to a stop in front of the glowing green wall.

7
00:00:36.227 --> 00:00:43.543
"You can't do this!" she yelled. Rubbing both hands together, she aimed a Blast spell at the shield.

8
00:00:43.544 --> 00:00:46.299
The blast bounced off and shot back at her.

9
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.308
She ducked, and it blew up a chair behind her.

10
00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:53.880
Morb threw back his head and laughed. "I should have used a shield sooner.

11
00:00:53.881 --> 00:00:56.758
That would have saved me a lot of trouble.

12
00:00:56.759 --> 00:01:01.116
But who could have guessed a few kids would be so hard to capture?

13
00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:07.486
In any case I've got you now." He turned and smirked at Zann.

14
00:01:07.487 --> 00:01:11.844
"Even you. Your grandfather is eager to see you.

15
00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:15.658
Perhaps you two can share a cell in my dungeon."

16
00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.450
Zann's heart pounded. "Now what?" he thought.

17
00:01:19.451 --> 00:01:24.548
They were truly trapped this time. Even Zing was shrinking away from Morb.

18
00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:28.767
As he looked around, desperate for ideas, Zann noticed something.

19
00:01:28.768 --> 00:01:33.693
That heavy wooden beam was still hanging in midair where his spell had frozen it.

20
00:01:33.694 --> 00:01:36.547
And Morb was just a few steps away!

21
00:01:36.548 --> 00:01:44.865
Zann gulped. Since early childhood he had been taught by his parents that one law in Magica was more important than any other.

22
00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:50.547
That law could be summed up in just a few simple words: Do no harm to others.

23
00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:53.555
But this was no time to worry about following the rules.

24
00:01:53.556 --> 00:01:58.477
He stepped sideways, so the beam now hung above the space between him and Morb.

25
00:01:58.478 --> 00:02:05.477
"Hey, Morb," he said. "I've got something to say to you—unless you're too scared to face a Red."

26
00:02:05.478 --> 00:02:09.384
Zann's friends looked startled, but Morb just chuckled.

27
00:02:09.385 --> 00:02:13.835
"Me, afraid of you?" Morb took a step toward Zann.

28
00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:20.348
"You obviously overestimate your own powers—just like your know-it-all grandfather."

29
00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:25.313
Morb took another step. The beam was now just above his head.

30
00:02:25.314 --> 00:02:30.529
If he looked up, he'd see it and move away. Zann had to act immediately.

31
00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.558
"Free," he whispered.

32
00:02:32.559 --> 00:02:36.209
The beam plummeted down and hit Morb square on the head.

33
00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:40.531
Morb grunted in surprise and crumpled to the ground, unconscious.

34
00:02:40.532 --> 00:02:44.009
As soon as Morb fell, the shield blinked out of sight.

35
00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.468
"Wow!" Perda cried. "That was great, Zann!"

36
00:02:48.469 --> 00:02:51.872
"Yeah. Let's get out of here!" Gliss added.

37
00:02:51.873 --> 00:02:57.566
Zing was already flying away from the ruined house. Darb, Perda, and Gliss followed.

38
00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.873
"Hurry, Zann!" Darb called.

39
00:02:59.874 --> 00:03:04.063
"Coming." Zann quickly reached under the table and grabbed the diary.

40
00:03:04.064 --> 00:03:07.867
Shoving it into his pocket, he raced after his friends.

41
00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.397
The group was soon back at the Hollow.

42
00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:14.615
"You don't think the beam killed Morb, do you?" Zann asked.

43
00:03:14.616 --> 00:03:19.970
"Definitely not," said Perda. "I saw him breathing when I ran past him."

44
00:03:19.971 --> 00:03:24.408
"But the way the shield just disappeared . . ." Zann began.

45
00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:27.748
"We learned about that in school," Gliss reminded him.

46
00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:32.009
"Certain types of spells require constant focus to maintain them.

47
00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.078
I guess it was one of those."

48
00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:41.230
"Don't worry, Zann," Darb said. "Even the do-no-harm-to-others rule makes an exception for emergencies."

49
00:03:41.231 --> 00:03:44.309
Zann flashed his friend a grateful smile.

50
00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:50.704
It was amazing how Darb could almost always guess what Zann was thinking, even without using any magic.

51
00:03:50.705 --> 00:03:56.888
"Okay," Zann said. "But that means Morb is going to be really angry when he wakes up.

52
00:03:56.889 --> 00:03:59.627
We'll have to be more careful than ever."

53
00:03:59.628 --> 00:04:04.235
Perda bit her lip. "He'll probably be watching for us at your house.

54
00:04:04.236 --> 00:04:07.446
How are we going to find that diary now?"

55
00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.741
"Oh!" Zann stuck his hand in his pocket.

56
00:04:10.742 --> 00:04:16.623
"I almost forgot—I found it." He pulled out the book. "That's the good news."

57
00:04:16.624 --> 00:04:19.566
"What's the bad news?" Perda asked.

58
00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:23.551
Zann grimaced. "It got damaged in the explosion."

59
00:04:23.552 --> 00:04:27.326
From the outside the diary appeared to be in pretty good shape.

60
00:04:27.327 --> 00:04:35.303
But as soon as Zann flipped it open, his friends could see that many of the interior pages were ripped, scorched, or missing altogether.

61
00:04:35.304 --> 00:04:41.471
"Wow," Perda said. "Do you think whatever Boz wanted the king and queen to see is still in there?"

62
00:04:41.472 --> 00:04:46.046
"Maybe I should read it and try to figure that out," Zann said.

63
00:04:46.047 --> 00:04:50.388
Gliss looked impatient. "We don't have time to sit around and read.

64
00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:53.510
We need to get that diary to the palace."

65
00:04:53.511 --> 00:04:56.769
"How are we supposed to do that?" Perda asked.

66
00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:02.482
"It would take days to reach First City on foot. And we can't use magic, remember?"

67
00:05:02.483 --> 00:05:08.789
"Plus traveling to the castle might not be worth the risk if the diary is damaged," Darb put in.

68
00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:15.003
"Zann's right. He should read it before we start a dangerous journey across Magica with Morb on our trail."

69
00:05:15.004 --> 00:05:21.694
"But we need to figure out what Morb is doing with my parents and all those other Reds," Gliss argued.

70
00:05:21.695 --> 00:05:27.937
"It seems like nobody else has ever even heard of Morb. Jev didn't recognize his name."

71
00:05:27.938 --> 00:05:32.064
Zann shrugged. "That's because Jev is an idiot."

72
00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:38.768
He expected Gliss to protest since she seemed to like Jev. Instead she looked thoughtful.

73
00:05:38.769 --> 00:05:43.354
"We could try sending a spy fly to spy on Morb," she suggested.

74
00:05:43.355 --> 00:05:48.325
"That might tell us what he's doing, and give Zann time to read the diary."

75
00:05:48.326 --> 00:05:53.189
"But we can't send a spy fly without magic," Perda reminded her.

76
00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.927
"And we can't use magic, or Morb will know exactly where we are."

77
00:05:57.928 --> 00:06:03.712
"We can't use magic," Gliss said. "But someone else could use it for us.

78
00:06:03.713 --> 00:06:06.357
Someone who isn't being tracked by Morb.

79
00:06:06.358 --> 00:06:09.526
And I know the perfect person for the job."

80
00:06:09.527 --> 00:06:11.619
"Who?" Zann asked.

81
00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:19.600
Gliss smiled. "Jev, of course."
